#### Persistent data

As mentioned earlier, the primary drive is erased every time the vmjail is recreated, so all data stored on it is lost and you have to start from scratch. The most practical solution is to use the secondary drive created by this AppJail to store the data you want to keep. However, you'll need to make some adjustments in Windows so that programs and user data are stored on the secondary drive. Fortunately, this can be done right in the generator mentioned earlier in the "Run custom scripts > `System` scripts" section.

1. ```bat
   mkdir D:\Users
   reg.exe add "HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\ProfileList" /v ProfilesDirectory /t REG_SZ /d "D:\Users" /f
   reg.exe add "HKLM\Software\WOW6432Node\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\ProfileList" /v ProfilesDirectory /t REG_SZ /d "D:\Users" /f
   ```

2. ```bat
   mkdir "D:\Program Files"
   mkdir "D:\Program Files (x86)"
   reg.exe add "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion" /v ProgramFilesDir /t REG_SZ /d "D:\Program Files" /f
   reg.exe add "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion" /v "ProgramFilesDir (x86)" /t REG_SZ /d "D:\Program Files (x86)" /f
   reg.exe add "HKLM\SOFTWARE\WOW6432Node\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion" /v ProgramFilesDir /t REG_SZ /d "D:\Program Files" /f
   ```

The only problem is that the `D:` drive might not be formatted. To avoid having to install Windows just to format the disk, you can run the `x11appjail create` command, create the disk image, and then use `mkntfs` from `filesystems/ntfs` to format it.

1. `x11appjail create appjail4win:win10`
2. `truncate -s 10G /var/x11appjail/users/15000/appjail4win.win10/data.img`
3. `md=$(doas mdconfig -at vnode -f /var/x11appjail/users/15000/appjail4win.win10/data.img)`
4. `doas gpart create -s gpt ${md}`
5. `doas gpart add -t ms-reserved -s 16M ${md}`
6. `doas gpart add -t ms-basic-data ${md}`
7. `doas env NTFS_USE_UBLIO=0 mkntfs -F -f -L "AppJail" /dev/${md}p2`
8. `doas mdconfig -du ${md}`

![](assets/img/win10-userdata.png)
